/target
**/*.rs.bk
Cargo.lock.bak

# Editor / OS
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp

# Local ledger artifacts
/assertions/
/checkpoints/
# Corpora are large and are distributed by hash, not by git. The provenance
# ABOUT them is the opposite: `/data/` used to hide data/README.md and the
# corpus manifest from `git add`, so the one file that lets a third party
# confirm they hold the same bytes could not be committed. Re-included by name;
# the derived and defective corpora stay ignored.
#
# `/data/*` and not `/data/`: git never descends into an EXCLUDED DIRECTORY, so
# a negation under `/data/` can never fire. Excluding the contents instead is
# what makes `!` work.
/data/*
!/data/README.md
!/data/MANIFEST.sha256
# The two corpora every reported BPB in this repository was measured against.
# 1.1 MB total, and tracking them is what makes the evidence chain survive its
# upstream: a hash detects SUBSTITUTION but cannot detect DELETION, so a pinned
# checksum whose preimage nobody holds tells an auditor they failed without
# telling them what the right bytes were. A conformity dossier has to stay
# re-checkable for the life of the certificate, which is longer than the life of
# a raw.githubusercontent.com path. Tracked copy is NORMATIVE; the curl in
# README.md is now a fallback. See data/README.md.
!/data/tiny_shakespeare.txt
!/data/tiny_shakespeare_val.txt
*.jsonl.tmp

# Training logs (thousands of files choke git)
.trinity/results/
.trinity/auto_launch.log
.trinity/gardener.log

# Build cache
.cargo/

# PDF pipeline artifacts
pdf-build/
pdf-output/
templates/
filters/

# Logs
LOG
$LOG
*.log
# ...except the ones that ARE the evidence. `docs/HELD-OUT-PROTOCOL.md` names
# `evidence/heldout/A.log` and `B.log` as the artifacts of the only held-out
# measurement this crate has made, and `*.log` silently kept them out of
# `git add -A` -- the same defect `/data/*` above was written to fix: the file
# that lets a third party check the claim was the one file that could not be
# committed. The negation fires here because no parent directory of these files
# is excluded (git never descends into an excluded directory).
!evidence/**/*.log

# History / eval artifacts
.trinity/history/

# Brochure outputs
trinity-brochure.pdf

# Constitution (generated)
trinity_constitution/

.env*
!.env.example
